### HubSpot Integration Service - example requests
### Open this file with the "REST Client" extension in VS Code, or copy
### each block into curl/Postman. See README.md for the full walkthrough.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Service info
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 1. Connect a HubSpot account - open this URL in a browser (not a plain
### request, since it's an interactive OAuth consent screen redirect)
# GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/hubspot/install

### Check connection status
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/hubspot/status

### 2. Trigger a full sync of contacts
POST {{baseUrl}}/sync/contacts

### Trigger a full sync of deals
POST {{baseUrl}}/sync/deals

### Sync both in one call
POST {{baseUrl}}/sync

### View recent sync run history
GET {{baseUrl}}/sync/runs?limit=10

### 3. List contacts from the local DB (filter + sort + paginate)
GET {{baseUrl}}/contacts?page=1&pageSize=25&sort=updatedAt:desc

### Filter contacts by email substring
GET {{baseUrl}}/contacts?email=example.com

### Filter contacts by lifecycle stage
GET {{baseUrl}}/contacts?lifecycleStage=lead

### Get one contact by local id
# GET {{baseUrl}}/contacts/<id>

### 4. List deals from the local DB
GET {{baseUrl}}/deals?page=1&pageSize=25&sort=amount:desc

### Filter deals by stage and amount range
GET {{baseUrl}}/deals?stage=closedwon&minAmount=1000&maxAmount=50000

### 5. Recent webhook deliveries received
GET {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/events?limit=20

### Retry processing a previously-failed webhook event
# POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/events/<id>/retry

### 6. Simulate a HubSpot webhook locally (bypasses signature check, dev only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/hubspot
Content-Type: application/json
X-Skip-Signature-Check: true

[
  {
    "eventId": 1,
    "subscriptionType": "contact.propertyChange",
    "objectId": 12345,
    "occurredAt": 1700000000000,
    "changeSource": "CRM",
    "propertyName": "lifecyclestage",
    "propertyValue": "customer"
  }
]

### For a *real* signed webhook test (no bypass header), run:
###   npm run test:webhook -- --type=contact.propertyChange --objectId=12345
